sycl: fuse the Inkling 2 short conv, depth mix, loop controller, L2 clip and situ chains

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0018.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

A port of CUDA's Inkling 2 fusions (#33060: ggml-cuda/inkling2.cu and the
matchers of fusion.cu) to ggml-sycl/inkling2.cpp. The graph emits these
chains in a fixed order, and ggml_sycl_fuse now tries them before top-k MoE:
- situ: the 10-node activation as one element-wise kernel;
- L2 clip: [MUL] L2_NORM SCALE [MUL] as one row kernel, in place;
- short conv: CONCAT, the conv-state store (CPY, or SET_ROWS with slots),
  SSM_CONV with its dynamic taps, ADD, SCALE and the residual ADD;
- depth mix: [RMS_NORM] CONCAT [REPEAT] MUL_MAT SOFT_MAX TRANSPOSE CONT
  MUL_MAT for up to 16 stacked rows, one work-group per token;
- loop controller: its 12 nodes as two kernels for up to 8 tokens.
Each matcher checks shapes, use counts and memory overlap as CUDA's does.
test-backend-ops SITU, L2_CLIP, SHORT_CONV, DEPTH_MIX and LOOP_CTRL pass on
the Arc Pro B60, and every case runs fused.

